SOLUTION_EXPLANATION: First, we calculate the volume of the living room. The room has a length of 4.0 m, a width of 5.0 m, and a height of 3.0 m. So, the volume (V) is:

V = length \(\times\) width \(\times\) height = 4.0 \(\times\) 5.0 \(\times\) 3.0 = 60.0 \text{ m}^3

Next, we find the mass of the air in this volume at \(20^{\circ} C\). The density of air at this temperature is about 1.204 kg/m³. Thus, the mass (m) of the air is:

m = density \(\times\) volume = 1.204 \(\times\) 60.0 = 72.24 \text{ kg}

The weight of the air (W) is calculated using the formula W = m \(\times\) g, where g is the acceleration due to gravity (approximately 9.81 m/s²):

W = 72.24 \(\times\) 9.81 = 708.6744 \text{ N} = 0.07086744 \text{ in units of } 10^5 \text{ N}

For water, we use its density of 1000 kg/m³. So the mass of water filling the same volume is:

m_water = density \(\times\) volume = 1000 \(\times\) 60.0 = 60000 \text{ kg}

The weight of this volume of water is:

W_water = 60000 \times 9.81 = 588600 \text{ N} = 5.886 \text{ in units of } 10^5 \text{ N}

Thus, the mass and weight of the air are 72.24 kg and approximately 0.0709×10^5 N, respectively, and the mass and weight of the water are 60000 kg and approximately 5.886×10^5 N, respectively.
ANSWER_AS_NUMBER: 5.886
